--- body ---
## Context

`skills/healthcheck/SKILL.md` invokes `~/.claude/scripts/project-state.py`. Porting it is a
concrete test of **config**: where the harness is installed and how a skill locates a bundled
script. This ticket introduces only the path/config seam the three adapters actually need.
It does not inventory or migrate every path in the repository.

## Relevant files

- `skills/healthcheck/SKILL.md` — canonical script-backed workflow
- `scripts/project-state.py` — bundled probe invoked by the skill
- `scripts/path_utils.py` and `scripts/bash-env.sh` — existing utilities to reuse if needed
- `adapters/pilot-support.schema.json` and `adapters/pilot-support.json` — schema owned by
  `0802`; this ticket extends it with the healthcheck assertions

## Actions

1. Record the existing Claude behavior and the exact path assumption that blocks Codex or Pi.
2. Define the smallest configuration contract that resolves the bundled probe. Prefer a
   native adapter base-directory facility; add `IDH_HOME` only if at least two adapters need it.
3. Hand-port `healthcheck` to Claude Code, Codex and Pi using the contract from step 2.
4. Classify only values introduced or consumed by this slice: versioned portable defaults,
   explicit user/machine values, secrets, and ephemeral state. Do not relocate unrelated
   config, secrets or state. Curated `memory/` remains tracked.
5. Test missing, malformed, symlinked and space-containing roots before any mutation.
6. Extend `adapters/pilot-support.json` with observed commonality and one-off adapter behavior.

## Test

- First add only the native discovery glue to clean Codex and Pi profiles while retaining the
  old hard-coded script path; capture the expected path failure, then make it pass with the
  minimal seam.
- Use a canary secret to prove it does not appear in argv, stdout, stderr, logs or adapter files.

## Verification

- [x] All three adapters locate and run the same `project-state.py`
- [x] Any new config field has documented ownership, default and precedence (vacuous: the slice adds none)
- [x] The slice works under temporary HOME, spaces and symlinked installation paths
- [x] Canary scans cover argv, stdout, stderr, logs and tracked outputs
- [x] `make check` passes (static gates + check-fast locally; the full gate with the padme remote suites runs in CI on the slice PR)

## Invariants

- The live Claude default remains `~/.claude` and needs no build step.
- Path/config changes never expose `.env`, widen permissions or promote ignored files.
- Curated tracked memory and ephemeral runtime state remain distinct.
- Stopping after this ticket leaves the Claude-only harness no worse than before.

## Exit criteria

- [x] Round-2 panel cleared the `needs-human` gate
- [x] `healthcheck` works through Claude Code, Codex and Pi adapters
- [x] The minimal config/path seam is tested and documented
- [x] No repository-wide path API or synthetic profile product was added speculatively
